      "has_manual": true,
      "summary": "Kaguguta Agrifarm recorded 5.6mm of rain in August 2026, roughly 0.1 times the long-term August average of around 48mm and well below normal for the month. Only two days registered measurable rain, and just one of them exceeded 1mm. The wettest day was 15 August with 5.0mm, followed by 26 Aug with 0.6mm, and no day reached the 10mm heavy-rain threshold. The first ten days of the month were entirely dry, the second dekad accounted for almost all of the total at 5.0mm, and the final dekad added 0.6mm. This dry outcome fits the Kenya Meteorological Department's August forecast, which called for generally sunny, dry weather with near-average to below-average rainfall across Kilifi and the neighbouring coastal counties."
