      "summary": "Kaguguta Agrifarm recorded 16.1mm of rain in September 2026, roughly half the long-term September average of around 35mm and well below normal for the month. Rain fell on only two days, and a single event accounted for nearly all of it: 15.0mm on 21 September, the month's only heavy-rain day, with 1.1mm on 12 September making up most of the remainder. The first dekad was entirely dry, the second recorded 1.1mm, and the final dekad delivered 15.0mm, so the month's rainfall was concentrated at the very end. This outcome ran below the Kenya Meteorological Department's early-September outlook, which had forecast near-average rainfall for Kilifi and the rest of the coast. KMD's review for 7 to 13 September noted that most of Kenya stayed dry, with rain confined to a few counties including Kilifi, while regional forecasters pointed to a developing El Niño and a positive Indian Ocean Dipole expected to continue through the final quarter of 2026, with a wetter-than-normal October to December season forecast for the Greater Horn of Africa."
