  "daily_narrative": "Kaguguta Agrifarm weather station in Kilifi County recorded no rainfall on 2, 3 and 4 October, and no reading was received for 5 October. The station has logged 0.0 mm so far this month and for the current dekad (Oct-D1), with one consecutive dry day noted in the report. The most recent measurable rainfall was 15.00 mm on 21 September, which is the largest daily total in the station's record since 1 August 2026. No ECMWF ensemble forecast was available at the time of reporting.",
  "dekadal_narrative": "The dekad recorded 15.0 mm, well above the 1.1 mm of Sep-D2; no Sep-D1 total is present in the record, so only one other dekad is available for comparison this month. All of the rain came from a single event on 21 September, which produced the full 15.0 mm and was the only rainy day of the dekad. The forecast for the coming dekad (6 to 15 October) is for a much wetter period, with a total of about 165.1 mm, the heaviest days expected around 12 and 13 October at 33.4 mm and 38.6 mm, and 8 October also forecast at 28.0 mm. On the regional side, the Kenya Meteorological Service declared the October to December short rains season begun, which fits the forecast increase in rainfall at the coast."
